# kufar-posting — the posting team's repository.
#
# The file sits in .github/ deliberately. GitHub reads CODEOWNERS only from the
# repository root, from .github/ or from docs/ — nested files like
# kufar.Foundation/CODEOWNERS are ignored silently. That is a legacy of the
# "repository = package" era, when every such file sat at its own root and
# worked. The location is checked by Tools/deplint.py, rule 11.
#
# Ownership inside the repository is split by PATHS: the contract package lists
# the platform team as a second owner, because a breaking change in a contract
# stops other teams. The last matching rule wins, and several owners mean OR —
# an approval from any one of them is enough.

